DATABASE_URL="file:./database/conversations.db"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Calendar connectors (Settings → Calendar)
#
# **Normal users do nothing here.** A shipped build carries the
# family-registered public client id (see
# `src/main/services/cloud/bundledClientIds.ts`), so the whole flow is:
# Settings → Calendar → "Sign in with Google" → browser consent → done.
#
# These variables are the OVERRIDE path — for self-hosters, forks and
# operators pointing a build at their own OAuth registration. Env wins over
# the bundled id.
#
# The flow is PKCE (RFC 8252 loopback). A client secret is not needed by the
# protocol — but Google's token endpoint requires one anyway for "Desktop app"
# clients, and Google documents it as NOT confidential for installed apps. So
# a shipped build bundles it as a public value, exactly like the client id
# (see `bundledClientIds.ts`). Only the resulting token is kept, in your OS
# keyring — never a credential in a config file.
#
# "needs configuration" on the Calendar tab means THIS build has no client id
# for that provider — bundled or env. It is a build/deployment setting, not
# something a user is expected to create.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Google Calendar — only if you are OVERRIDING the bundled id ──────────
# 1. https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials → Create credentials →
#    OAuth client ID → Application type: **Desktop app**.
# 2. Enable the API: https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library/calendar-json.googleapis.com
# 3. OAuth consent screen: add yourself as a test user (unpublished apps
#    refuse anyone not on that list).
# 4. Paste the client ID here and restart (the bundled id is used otherwise).
#
# The app requests exactly two scopes, shown verbatim before you consent:
#   …/auth/calendar.readonly   read your schedule
#   …/auth/calendar.events     create / move events
# DESKTOP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""
# Google only: the (non-confidential) desktop client value, if you registered
# your own client. Bundled otherwise.
# DESKTOP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# ── Microsoft 365 — only if you are OVERRIDING the bundled id ────────────
# 1. https://portal.azure.com → App registrations → New registration →
#    Supported account types: the one matching your tenant (often
#    "Accounts in this organizational directory only").
# 2. Authentication → Add a platform → **Mobile and desktop applications** →
#    add the redirect URI `http://127.0.0.1` (the app uses a loopback
#    redirect per RFC 8252 and picks an ephemeral port).
# 3. API permissions → Microsoft Graph → Delegated → `Calendars.Read`,
#    `Calendars.ReadWrite`, `User.Read`, `offline_access` → **Grant admin
#    consent** if your tenant requires it.
# 4. Paste the Application (client) ID here and restart.
# DESKTOP_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=""
